    "name": "crop map of england crome and rpa ground observation points",
    "url": "https://www.data.gov.uk/dataset/0f52fe52-80f6-4aa7-bee2-afb9a320f631/crop-map-of-england-crome-2024"
  },
  "description": "The Crop Map of England (CROME) is an annual Rural Payments Agency vector map of crop types. The 2024 edition has about 32 million hexagonal cells classifying England into over 15 main crop types, grassland and non-agricultural covers such as woodland, water, fallow and other land. It is produced by Random Forest classification of Sentinel-1 radar time series (January to August 2024), so it is not blocked by cloud, and is checked against field surveys and visual validation. Data are split by ceremonial county, with a land use code lookup and a specification document. Editions exist from 2016 (first by region) to 2024. The RPA Ground Observation Points, kept since 2015, record crop or land cover, date and surveyor at sample parcels; the 2024 set has over 11,000 fixed locations in 32 zones and adds mowing and harvest events. Both are free under the Open Government Licence, with downloads, WMS, WFS and OGC API Features services from the Environment Agency data service. Caveats: the map is a classification with errors, and the observation points are a sample. For simulation it gives field-level crop maps to estimate agricultural exposure to floods, droughts and heat, and crop-specific water, energy and transport demand. Related catalogue records include the USDA Cropland Data Layer and the JRC EUCROPMAP.",
  "description_checked": "2026-09-26",
